@flexiarg operator/measure-footing-against-a-past-baseline
@title Measure The Current Footing Against A Named Past Baseline
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-5ZOY3w turn-ZbpMfj; first proposed for: Work has just been approved and the operator takes stock of how much the project now has to go on.
@why [peeragogy/par]

! conclusion: State the comparison against a specific dated point — the creation of a named earlier mission — so the footing gain is inspectable.

  + IF:
    He says 'we have a lot more to go on … than we did when X was created', naming the earlier mission as the baseline.

  + HOWEVER:
    Progress felt without a baseline is unfalsifiable optimism; a baseline named too loosely ('things are better') cannot be checked either.

  + THEN:
    State the comparison against a specific dated point — the creation of a named earlier mission — so the footing gain is inspectable.

  + BECAUSE:
    A PAR-style review establishes what is happening against an intention or earlier state; naming the baseline mission turns the review's 'more to go on' into a checkable claim about two corpus states.
